r-core forcing will help.; Avoid shotgun tuning (simultaneously changing tile sizes, warps, stages, and control knobs) in a single round.; Avoid assuming tensor-core/MFMA path automatically improves performance without checking occupancy and launch efficiency.; Avoid dropping explicit tuning knobs to None unless there is evidence autotuned defaults are better for this workload.- PRIORITIZE: Keep MFMA enabled but perform a focused autotune sweep over BLOCK_M/N/K, num_warps, and waves_per_eu.; Reintroduce or tune grouping/scheduling controls (e.g., GROUP_M) to improve locality and wave balance.; Profile shape-specific kernels and choose separate configs for small/latency-sensitive vs larger/throughput-oriented workloads.; Run controlled A/B tests: keep launch params fixed while toggling only VALU vs MFMA lowering, then tune waves_per_eu/register pressure separately.; Profile deeper counters (occupancy, VGPR usage, MFMA issue rate, stall reasons, instruction mix) to confirm whether compute units are efficiently utilized.; Explore shape-specific tiling/k-pack/block-size choices that better match MFMA fragment sizes before broad kernel rewrites.; Run controlled ablations: test matrix_instr_nonkdim, BLOCK_K, BLOCK_N, and waves_per_eu independently, then combine only winning changes.; Confirm actual MFMA issuance and occupancy/register behavior with profiler counters before and after each change.; Search around smaller/local tile variants (e.g., keep one dimension fixed) and tune num_warps/num_stages for better pipeline balance.; Evaluate precision/layout variants that preserve MFMA while reducing register pressure and improving wave residency.; A/B test minimal deltas: keep prior-good tiling and only toggle MFMA-related codegen options.; Run structured autotuning around BLOCK_M/N/K, num_warps/waves_per_eu, and stages specifically for CDNA3 MFMA shapes.; Profile for limiting sub-metrics (e.g., occupancy, VALU/MFMA utilization, register spills, latency stalls) before and after each micro-change.; Run an ablation study: first force/verify MFMA with minimal tile changes, then tune BLOCK_M/N/K one parameter at a time.; Test a smaller set of balanced tiles (e.g., moderate BLOCK_M/N with current BLOCK_K) to preserve occupancy while using MFMA.; Sweep num_warps and num_stages separately (e.g., keep warps fixed while varying stages) and track register pressure/active waves.; Use problem-size-aware tiling and ensure tile dimensions align with MFMA fragment shapes without over-inflating per-CTA resource use.\\n\\n## PERFORMANCE TARGET\\n- PyTorch Eager baseline: 0.0149 ms\\n- Current best kernel: 0.0214 ms\\n- Target: Improve by at least 10% (< 0.0193 ms)\\n- Maintain numerical correctness (atol=1e-4 or rtol=1e-4)\\n- Preserve public API (same inputs/outputs, shapes, dtypes)\\n\\n## REQUIREMENTS\\n1. Apply the recommended fixes above to address the COMPUTE bottleneck\\n2. The implementation must be a complete, valid Python file\\n3. Main function must be named 'kernel_function' wrapping the Triton kernel\\n4. Keep the wrapper free of PyTorch compute primitives\\n\\n## OUTPUT FORMAT\\nOutput complete optimized kernel code in ```python blocks.\\nInclude only: imports, Triton kernel (@triton.jit), wrapper function (kernel_function).\\nNo testing code, benchmarks, or explanatory comments.\\n\\nGenerate the complete optimized kernel implementation:\"}]}],\"max_output_tokens\":24576,\"model\":\"gpt-5.3-codex\",\"reasoning\":{\"effort\":\"high\"}}"}}, "request_meta": {"model": "gpt-5.3-codex", "max_output_tokens": 24576, "reasoning": {"effort": "high"}}, "response": {"http_version": "HTTP/1.1", "headers": [["Date", "Thu, 12 Mar 2026 08:04:26 GMT"], ["Content-Type", "application/json"], ["Transfer-Encoding", "chunked"], ["Connection", "keep-alive"], ["Server", "cloudflare"], ["x-ratelimit-limit-requests", "15000"], ["x-ratelimit-limit-tokens", "40000000"], ["x-ratelimit-remaining-requests", "14999"], ["x-ratelimit-remaining-tokens", "39990398"], ["x-r